1
00:00:15,216 --> 00:00:17,510
- Merry Christmas!
- Merry Christmas!

2
00:00:17,510 --> 00:00:18,553
Merry Christmas.

3
00:00:18,553 --> 00:00:19,804
Merry Christmas.

4
00:00:20,657 --> 00:00:21,950
Thank you for bringing me here.

5
00:00:21,985 --> 00:00:23,820
I told you you’d have a good time here.

6
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:25,446
And I’m glad you’re happy.

7
00:00:26,781 --> 00:00:28,575
I’m not part of your family.

8
00:00:28,575 --> 00:00:30,076
I’ll just take the picture.

9
00:00:30,076 --> 00:00:32,370
Well, you’re a part of my life now, right?

10
00:00:32,579 --> 00:00:33,663
So go on, wear it.

11
00:00:33,997 --> 00:00:35,540
Theo! You’re here.

12
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:36,624
- Come on, don’t be shy.
- Ke.

13
00:00:37,584 --> 00:00:39,002
You’re the barista from the coffee shop.

14
00:00:39,002 --> 00:00:41,129
And you’re the one who spilled coffee
at the coffee shop.

15
00:00:42,297 --> 00:00:44,549
Aren’t you jealous of him?

16
00:00:44,757 --> 00:00:45,692
No.

17
00:00:45,717 --> 00:00:47,302
You’re gonna stop hanging out with them

18
00:00:48,011 --> 00:00:49,554
and you’re not gonna see them anymore.

19
00:00:49,554 --> 00:00:50,400
What about you?

20
00:00:51,589 --> 00:00:52,715
Aren’t you the jealous type?

21
00:00:53,992 --> 00:00:55,785
Are you trying to make me jealous?

22
00:00:55,810 --> 00:00:56,769
No.

23
00:00:57,816 --> 00:00:58,900
I would never.

24
00:00:58,925 --> 00:01:01,594
Do you want to spend New Year’s with us?

25
00:01:01,619 --> 00:01:02,829
Celebrate with us.

26
00:01:04,110 --> 00:01:05,063
Sure.

27
00:01:09,783 --> 00:01:12,869
- Happy New Year!
- Happy New Year!

28
00:02:45,545 --> 00:02:46,504
You look happier.

29
00:02:47,380 --> 00:02:48,214
Really?

30
00:02:48,548 --> 00:02:49,340
So much happier.

31
00:02:50,154 --> 00:02:51,906
Can you tell me more about him?

32
00:02:53,216 --> 00:02:53,925
Well,

33
00:02:55,616 --> 00:02:58,161
I like who I become when I'm with him.

34
00:03:00,393 --> 00:03:02,228
He makes me feel safe.

35
00:03:04,147 --> 00:03:05,106
At peace.

36
00:03:06,691 --> 00:03:07,900
And I'm happy.

37
00:03:12,373 --> 00:03:13,207
Celebrate with us.

38
00:03:13,406 --> 00:03:15,366
Here in Bataan again, or in Manila?

39
00:03:15,450 --> 00:03:18,953
Shan, you’ll enjoy it even more once
you find out where we’re going.

40
00:04:05,958 --> 00:04:09,087
Oh my god, we're here!

41
00:04:09,670 --> 00:04:11,255
- Let's take a picture first.
- It's so cold!

42
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:12,965
Let's take a picture first.

43
00:04:12,965 --> 00:04:13,966
- Ready.
- A picture?

44
00:04:13,966 --> 00:04:14,675
Mhmm.

45
00:04:14,675 --> 00:04:16,177
One, two, three—

46
00:05:49,145 --> 00:05:50,744
They're still so sweet, huh?

47
00:05:51,412 --> 00:05:54,248
Still in love, after so many years.

48
00:06:05,077 --> 00:06:06,037
Hey.

49
00:06:06,037 --> 00:06:06,954
Where should we go?

50
00:06:06,979 --> 00:06:08,981
- Over there.
- Want to see who gets more?

51
00:06:09,123 --> 00:06:09,957
You in?

52
00:06:09,957 --> 00:06:10,458
Are you?

53
00:06:10,458 --> 00:06:11,667
- Okay.
- I'll be over here.

54
00:08:10,536 --> 00:08:11,454
You good?

55
00:08:12,538 --> 00:08:13,748
Yeah. How about you?

56
00:09:50,136 --> 00:09:51,470
I can't find my jacket.

57
00:09:53,821 --> 00:09:55,615
I can't remember where I put it.

58
00:09:58,547 --> 00:09:59,914
Just wear this for now.

59
00:10:01,305 --> 00:10:02,822
Just enjoy.

60
00:10:07,479 --> 00:10:10,816
Don't worry, we'll figure
something out. We'll look for it.

61
00:10:21,964 --> 00:10:23,466
One, two, three—

62
00:10:23,877 --> 00:10:25,504
I look so grumpy in this.

63
00:10:26,201 --> 00:10:27,869
You look like a grumpy old man.

64
00:10:32,674 --> 00:10:34,842
- But yeah, you're right.
- You look like a grumpy old man.

65
00:10:36,118 --> 00:10:39,163
You actually look like a grandma
who loves playing bingo.

66
00:10:39,477 --> 00:10:40,436
Seriously?

67
00:10:40,436 --> 00:10:42,313
The one who shouts bingo at the—

68
00:10:43,255 --> 00:10:44,298
Oh, really…

69
00:10:45,357 --> 00:10:47,401
Okay. I'm saving this, okay?

70
00:10:47,863 --> 00:10:49,782
I'm saving this so...

71
00:10:58,301 --> 00:10:59,969
Come on, Grandma,
you've still got bingo to play.

72
00:11:11,483 --> 00:11:12,276
Is it good?

73
00:11:12,301 --> 00:11:15,137
Their coffee here is so good.
I'm sure Shan would love it.

74
00:11:15,631 --> 00:11:17,090
Good to hear.

75
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:18,516
Hold on.

76
00:11:18,516 --> 00:11:19,183
Hmm?

77
00:11:19,183 --> 00:11:20,142
What did they go back for, anyway?

78
00:11:20,142 --> 00:11:23,604
We made it up, Mommy, so we could
get everything ready for the surprise.

79
00:11:23,813 --> 00:11:26,982
- Oh, right.
- Oh. Here they come.

80
00:11:26,982 --> 00:11:28,526
- They're here.
- They're here?

81
00:11:28,526 --> 00:11:30,486
Is this your surprise?

82
00:11:40,454 --> 00:11:42,456
Happy Birthday!

83
00:11:43,624 --> 00:11:46,001
[in Korean]
Happy birthday to you—

84
00:11:46,001 --> 00:11:48,087
♪ Happy birthday to you— ♪

85
00:11:48,087 --> 00:11:50,923
♪ Happy birthday, dear Shan… ♪

86
00:11:51,402 --> 00:11:53,342
♪ Happy birthday to you. ♪

87
00:11:59,723 --> 00:12:00,933
Happy Birthday.

88
00:12:00,933 --> 00:12:03,435
- Happy Birthday!
- Happy Birthday!

89
00:12:03,856 --> 00:12:04,979
Thank you.

90
00:12:04,979 --> 00:12:09,775
From now on, we're always going
to celebrate your birthday happily.

91
00:12:09,775 --> 00:12:10,860
No exceptions.

92
00:12:13,070 --> 00:12:15,030
Why do you look like
you're about to cry?

93
00:12:15,030 --> 00:12:15,614
Huh?

94
00:12:15,639 --> 00:12:16,824
- Are you crying?
- No.

95
00:12:16,824 --> 00:12:19,243
- No, I'm not, really.
- Hey, don't cry.

96
00:12:19,882 --> 00:12:21,245
I'm the one with a surprise for you.

97
00:12:21,245 --> 00:12:21,620
Huh?

98
00:12:21,620 --> 00:12:22,580
- Why?
- Here, look.

99
00:12:23,490 --> 00:12:25,576
Surprise!

100
00:12:26,250 --> 00:12:28,294
He really went back to check everywhere.

101
00:12:28,368 --> 00:12:29,828
Because he said it's your favorite.

102
00:12:29,968 --> 00:12:31,630
He’s so dramatic, Mommy.

103
00:12:31,655 --> 00:12:33,869
I gave her that, that's
why it's her favorite.

104
00:12:34,356 --> 00:12:35,857
Thank you. Thank you so much.

105
00:12:42,224 --> 00:12:43,183
You guys go first.

106
00:12:48,772 --> 00:12:49,315
Selfie.

107
00:12:50,190 --> 00:12:50,983
Selfie.

108
00:12:54,403 --> 00:12:56,947
Happy Birthday!

109
00:13:13,631 --> 00:13:16,508
Oh, I actually bought
something for you earlier.

110
00:13:16,508 --> 00:13:17,635
Here.

111
00:13:17,843 --> 00:13:18,969
What's that?

112
00:13:18,969 --> 00:13:20,888
I saw it and thought it
would look good on you.

113
00:13:20,888 --> 00:13:21,388
Here.

114
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:24,433
It's so pretty. Let's put it on.

115
00:13:31,148 --> 00:13:33,150
You got one too? Thank you!

116
00:14:53,981 --> 00:14:55,274
It's so nice!

117
00:15:11,190 --> 00:15:14,485
- Happy New Year.
- Happy New Year.

118
00:15:14,510 --> 00:15:16,929
- Happy New Year.
- Happy New Year.

119
00:15:20,299 --> 00:15:22,051
- Happy New Year to all of us.
- Happy New Year.

120
00:15:22,051 --> 00:15:23,719
- Happy New Year.
- Happy New Year!

121
00:15:23,719 --> 00:15:25,763
- Happy New Year.
- Happy New, Shan

122
00:15:32,306 --> 00:15:33,140
It's so cold.

123
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:35,606
Oh.

124
00:15:35,939 --> 00:15:37,357
- Happy New Year hug.
- Wait a minute.

125
00:15:37,357 --> 00:15:37,816
Yeah?

126
00:15:37,816 --> 00:15:38,650
What's that?

127
00:15:38,650 --> 00:15:39,318
What?

128
00:15:39,318 --> 00:15:39,985
That.

129
00:15:40,944 --> 00:15:41,820
Here you go.

130
00:15:44,615 --> 00:15:45,532
Thank you.

131
00:15:46,075 --> 00:15:46,492
Yeah.

132
00:15:46,780 --> 00:15:48,114
Let's go eat.

133
00:15:49,059 --> 00:15:51,103
So we'll be full all year round.

134
00:15:56,794 --> 00:15:58,128
Happy New Year, Ayi.

135
00:16:01,590 --> 00:16:03,759
I'm happy to start the new year with you.

136
00:16:05,768 --> 00:16:07,668
I'm happy to be with you, too.

137
00:16:09,098 --> 00:16:10,349
Happy New Year.

138
00:16:22,486 --> 00:16:23,070
Hey.

139
00:16:23,070 --> 00:16:23,904
- Hey.
- Hm?

140
00:16:23,904 --> 00:16:24,655
Someone’s call—

141
00:16:24,655 --> 00:16:25,280
Hey!

142
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:25,697
Hey.

143
00:16:26,490 --> 00:16:28,784
- We said we'd call each other.
- They're going to greet us—

144
00:16:28,784 --> 00:16:29,910
Let's go inside, the
signal's weak out here.

145
00:16:38,168 --> 00:16:40,212
What's your New Year's wish?

146
00:16:43,423 --> 00:16:47,803
I know it's impossible
not to feel fear or pain,

147
00:16:48,470 --> 00:16:51,932
so I'll just wish for the universe
to start being kind to me.

148
00:16:54,351 --> 00:16:55,227
How about you?

149
00:17:02,317 --> 00:17:04,653
I wish to have more yesterdays with you.

150
00:17:05,237 --> 00:17:06,655
Not tomorrows?

151
00:17:08,365 --> 00:17:09,908
Yesterday's already the past.

152
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:13,579
Mhmm. Yesterday.

153
00:17:15,747 --> 00:17:18,041
Because that's the only thing
in this world that's certain.

154
00:17:20,377 --> 00:17:21,503
Right.

155
00:17:32,431 --> 00:17:34,975
I may not promise you my tomorrow.

156
00:17:37,060 --> 00:17:40,105
But I will certainly
promise you my yesterday.

157
00:17:45,277 --> 00:17:46,486
Forever...

158
00:17:47,696 --> 00:17:48,947
and beyond.

159
00:22:52,472 --> 00:22:53,848
You can't sleep?

160
00:22:56,463 --> 00:22:57,380
No.

161
00:23:01,728 --> 00:23:04,622
Did you feel uncomfortable earlier?

162
00:23:06,985 --> 00:23:08,336
No, not like that.

163
00:23:19,396 --> 00:23:21,114
When someone says "love,"

164
00:23:24,746 --> 00:23:26,734
what do you imagine?

165
00:23:32,290 --> 00:23:38,755
Daddy told me he tried to paint Mommy once,
but he never finished it.

166
00:23:40,340 --> 00:23:41,341
Why not?

167
00:23:43,468 --> 00:23:48,682
Because he said he could never
give justice to how lovely she was.

168
00:23:51,226 --> 00:23:56,147
That the existing colors just
couldn’t reflect the way he saw her.

169
00:23:56,773 --> 00:23:59,568
And he would never be
satisfied with his work—

170
00:24:00,735 --> 00:24:05,198
because no canvas was enough to
fit all the good qualities my mom had.

171
00:24:07,784 --> 00:24:09,452
Then he also said,

172
00:24:10,829 --> 00:24:15,834
that loving someone means going
beyond what you're already capable of.

173
00:24:20,589 --> 00:24:27,262
But he said that when love is healthy,
it should still make you feel full.

174
00:24:28,805 --> 00:24:31,474
Because when you feel
like you're being drained...

175
00:24:33,935 --> 00:24:37,355
Maybe you’re no longer going beyond.

176
00:24:39,608 --> 00:24:42,736
Maybe you’re already
losing yourself behind.

177
00:24:45,030 --> 00:24:47,449
And love shouldn't be like that.

178
00:24:49,242 --> 00:24:53,747
Because if it were,
you'd just get tired and hurt.

179
00:24:55,624 --> 00:24:57,959
That's how I felt back then.

180
00:25:10,180 --> 00:25:11,931
I like how your dad put it.

181
00:25:22,282 --> 00:25:23,742
Want to go out?

182
00:25:25,695 --> 00:25:27,614
It seems…

183
00:25:28,198 --> 00:25:30,283
nice to have hot chocolate right now.

184
00:25:31,576 --> 00:25:33,370
It's the middle of the night.

185
00:25:34,621 --> 00:25:36,331
But we're in Korea.

186
00:25:41,461 --> 00:25:44,339
I hope we can go back here someday.

187
00:25:45,674 --> 00:25:48,551
But I want to try other countries too.

188
00:25:48,944 --> 00:25:51,345
But Jeju is already special to me.

189
00:25:52,681 --> 00:25:54,099
Because I’m here with you?

190
00:25:54,124 --> 00:25:55,501
Oh, whatever.

191
00:26:00,355 --> 00:26:01,356
What are you doing?

192
00:26:03,055 --> 00:26:04,222
I'm leaving it here.

193
00:26:05,151 --> 00:26:09,906
So we'll have a reason to come back
years from now, right?

194
00:26:13,785 --> 00:26:15,704
It might be gone by the time we come back.

195
00:26:16,133 --> 00:26:21,138
Well, maybe it'll be gone physically,
but that doesn't mean it's gone.

196
00:26:22,794 --> 00:26:25,672
Absence doesn't erase existence, right?

197
00:26:30,927 --> 00:26:32,178
I want some hot chocolate.

198
00:26:32,762 --> 00:26:33,972
It's so cold.

199
00:26:54,033 --> 00:26:54,909
Are you okay?

200
00:26:56,035 --> 00:26:58,580
Baby, does it hurt?

201
00:26:58,580 --> 00:26:59,456
Is it okay?

202
00:27:01,149 --> 00:27:03,026
What? Do you want a kiss?

203
00:27:03,543 --> 00:27:05,003
That’s not what I meant.

204
00:27:11,885 --> 00:27:15,263
Do you think you'd
want to fall in love again?

205
00:27:17,528 --> 00:27:19,822
When I look at my parents,

206
00:27:21,686 --> 00:27:24,230
I still believe that love is beautiful.

207
00:27:25,440 --> 00:27:31,988
Despite everything that happened, I
still want to experience that kind of love.

208
00:27:34,035 --> 00:27:38,039
And I hope it's not too late for me.

209
00:27:43,833 --> 00:27:44,876
It's not too late.

210
00:27:46,711 --> 00:27:50,048
I used to think it was over for me, too.

211
00:27:51,132 --> 00:27:56,054
Imagine, I grew up with parents
who didn't love each other.

212
00:27:57,722 --> 00:28:02,060
If they weren't capable of feeling love,
then how could I?

213
00:28:04,979 --> 00:28:08,316
You know what, if you had
asked me before what love is,

214
00:28:08,566 --> 00:28:12,654
my answer would've just
come from a dictionary.

215
00:28:14,871 --> 00:28:16,081
But now?

216
00:28:18,560 --> 00:28:24,066
But now, I think love is...

217
00:28:27,500 --> 00:28:28,667
love is...

218
00:28:31,575 --> 00:28:33,536
I can't describe it in words.

219
00:28:38,680 --> 00:28:46,145
But every time I'm with you, I feel
something that makes me understand it.

220
00:28:54,776 --> 00:28:56,444
I’m in love with you, Ke.

221
00:29:02,495 --> 00:29:03,955
And I’m going beyond.

222
00:29:16,801 --> 00:29:18,678
You don't have to say it back.

223
00:29:19,404 --> 00:29:20,405
I’m sorry.

224
00:29:20,603 --> 00:29:21,436
No.

225
00:29:23,683 --> 00:29:26,895
I'm happy and hopeful.

226
00:29:30,725 --> 00:29:32,143
I'm just scared.

227
00:29:39,677 --> 00:29:41,137
Not for me.

228
00:29:42,619 --> 00:29:43,745
For you.

229
00:29:48,482 --> 00:29:50,609
‘Cause you’re loving someone like me.

230
00:29:55,757 --> 00:29:57,008
Yeah.

231
00:29:59,260 --> 00:30:00,845
Someone as lovely as you.

232
00:30:02,933 --> 00:30:04,727
Someone as sweet as you.

233
00:30:07,685 --> 00:30:09,854
And someone who has
a beautiful soul like you.

234
00:30:15,109 --> 00:30:17,946
If you could only see
yourself through my eyes,

235
00:30:22,640 --> 00:30:24,683
then you would feel the same way, too.

236
00:30:30,567 --> 00:30:32,523
I wish I could say it back to you.

237
00:30:35,713 --> 00:30:40,510
I just want to be
a hundred percent when I say it.

238
00:30:41,594 --> 00:30:43,930
Because I want to be fair to you.

239
00:30:46,933 --> 00:30:50,937
I'll wait until you're ready.

240
00:30:54,440 --> 00:30:56,734
Even if it takes until my next life.

241
00:31:18,381 --> 00:31:20,508
And before you say it to me,

242
00:31:21,842 --> 00:31:24,344
I want you to say it
to yourself first, okay?

243
00:31:28,516 --> 00:31:30,810
Because you deserve to be loved.

244
00:31:32,311 --> 00:31:36,691
By your friends, by your family—

245
00:31:38,317 --> 00:31:39,444
by me.

246
00:31:41,070 --> 00:31:42,905
And most especially

247
00:31:43,704 --> 00:31:45,038
by yourself.

248
00:32:02,091 --> 00:32:04,802
So, what do you call these feelings?

249
00:32:08,973 --> 00:32:10,516
Do you still love me?

250
00:32:11,342 --> 00:32:13,677
Yes. I love you.

251
00:32:14,353 --> 00:32:15,563
Always.

252
00:32:17,315 --> 00:32:18,649
Do you love me?

253
00:32:21,565 --> 00:32:23,327
It's still hard to say.

254
00:32:24,238 --> 00:32:27,909
How about what you're feeling for yourself?

255
00:32:31,961 --> 00:32:34,756
I can finally look at myself in the mirror.

256
00:32:36,542 --> 00:32:40,630
Without being disgusted with myself.

257
00:32:43,549 --> 00:32:46,427
I can finally be happy
without feeling guilty.

258
00:32:49,180 --> 00:32:52,225
I feel hopeful for myself.

259
00:32:55,228 --> 00:32:59,398
And I feel like I wanna make
relationships with people again.

260
00:33:03,945 --> 00:33:08,616
For the first time in a long time,
I don't…

261
00:33:09,826 --> 00:33:11,911
I don’t hate myself anymore.

262
00:33:16,415 --> 00:33:19,293
That is a very nice thing to say, Kierra.

263
00:33:22,588 --> 00:33:24,674
Your love is yours to give.

264
00:33:27,093 --> 00:33:29,887
Don’t allow anyone to
take it away from you.

265
00:33:32,682 --> 00:33:36,686
And whoever receives love
from someone as brave as you—

266
00:33:37,937 --> 00:33:40,064
will be a very lucky person.

267
00:33:43,818 --> 00:33:45,194
Remember that, okay?

268
00:33:46,654 --> 00:33:49,490
